From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] directmanipulation: viewports, contents, manipulation, inertia, updates

Direct Manipulation was a shell: almost every method of the viewport,
its contents, the manager, the update manager and the compositor was a
FIXME that returned E_NOTIMPL or did nothing, so a program that hands its
pointers to a viewport (as XAML-style scroll views and browsers' touch
paths do) never saw its content move or its status change.

- Viewports: status (building, enabled, disabled, running, inertia,
  ready) told to their event handlers (OnViewportStatusChanged,
  OnContentUpdated per content, OnViewportUpdated) and interaction
  handlers (begin, manipulation or pinch, end); Enable, Disable, Stop,
  Abandon; viewport rect, viewport and display transforms; tags;
  configurations (added, removed, activated, checked), viewport options,
  manual gestures, chaining, input and update modes; secondary contents;
  behaviors.
- The primary content's transform (a scale and a translation): content
  rect, zoom boundaries and alignments keep it in the viewport;
  ZoomToRect (at once, or animated); SyncContentTransform; snap
  intervals and points (mandatory and optional, per motion, with their
  coordinates); GetInertiaEndTransform, GetCenterPoint, the output
  transform (secondary contents follow the primary's translation).
- Manipulation: the contacts a program sets (SetContact) pan the content
  (one pointer, along rails if asked) and zoom it about the pointers'
  centre (two or more), from the activated window's pointer messages
  (automatic input: the window does not see them) or ProcessInput
  (manual); lifted, the content goes on with inertia and rests on a snap
  point. Animations advance on a timer of the activated window, or on
  the update manager's Update; RegisterWaitHandleCallback calls its
  handler whenever the handle is signalled.
- The compositor puts the contents' output transforms on their
  DirectComposition visuals and commits them when flushed; its frame
  information gives the frame's times.

Wine's directmanipulation tests: as before.

Gate: test/dmanip-gate.sh (Xvfb, test/dmanip-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_CONTENT_EVENTS, SG_MUTANT_NO_POINTER_INPUT,
SG_MUTANT_NO_UPDATE (directmanipulation/directmanipulation.c).
