+/* Stained Glass OS 1668: Direct Manipulation.
+ *
+ * A viewport shows its primary content through a transform (a scale and a
+ * translation, matrix [s 0 0 s tx ty]) that the user changes with the
+ * pointers the program hands it (SetContact) -- panning with one, zooming
+ * with two, within the configuration it activated -- and that goes on by
+ * itself after they lift (inertia) and settles on the snap points. Its
+ * event handlers hear of its status (enabled, running, inertia, ready, ...)
+ * and of each content update. Pointer input reaches the viewport through
+ * the activated window (automatic input) or ProcessInput (manual);
+ * animations advance on a timer of the window or on the update manager's
+ * Update. The compositor puts the transforms on DirectComposition
+ * visuals. */
